</section>

<section class="section section--line" id="integration-approach" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--split">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>Our approach</span>
        <h2 id="approach-heading">Most integration problems are governance problems</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal" style="--d:1">Two systems holding the same record will eventually disagree. The question is what happens next. Without a defined source of truth, conflicting updates overwrite each other silently and nobody notices until reporting is wrong. We decide which system owns which field before we build anything, then add the logging and alerting that makes failures visible.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-3" data-stagger>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-key" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h3>Defined ownership</h3><p>Every synced field has one system of record. Conflicts resolve by rule, not by whichever update landed last.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-icon card-icon--blue"><i class="fa-solid fa-bell" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h3>Visible failures</h3><p>Sync errors trigger alerts rather than sitting in a log nobody opens. You find out when something breaks.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><div class="card-icon card-icon--green"><i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-left" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h3>Reversible changes</h3><p>Bulk syncs run in a sandbox first and ship with a rollback path. A bad mapping does not become a data recovery project.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="integration-process" aria-labelledby="iprocess-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--center reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>How it works</span>
      <h2 id="iprocess-heading">From stack audit to live sync</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="timeline timeline--3" role="list">
      <li class="step reveal"><div class="step__num">01</div><h3>Audit your stack</h3><p>Map every tool, what data moves between them, and where it currently breaks. Identify duplicated data entry and governance gaps.</p></li>
      <li class="step reveal" style="--d:1"><div class="step__num">02</div><h3>Design the data flow</h3><p>Define the source of truth for each field, the mapping and transformation logic, and how errors are handled. All of it written down.</p></li>
      <li class="step reveal" style="--d:2"><div class="step__num">03</div><h3>Build, test, monitor</h3><p>Build in a sandbox, test against real data, deploy with monitoring and alerts, then document it so your team knows what runs where.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

